// The talisman bearer's recall. Granted to whoever carries a bonded talisman
// (never to the Warlock) and withdrawn the instant the bond drops.
//
// Deliberately bearer-activated rather than a reactive yank on damage: a
// Warlock able to rip an ally out of their own fight, with an item the ally
// cannot discard mid-combat, is a griefing vector with no counterplay.
//
// `anchor` is what makes it a recall rather than an ordinary blink -- it goes
// to the source of the bond buff, never to whatever the bearer is aiming at.
// It is still the same `Blink` state, so a dimensional anchor
// (`Stats.disable_teleport`) fizzles it exactly as it fizzles every other
// teleport.
//
// `max_range` and `cooldown` mirror `assets/common/pact/talisman_tuning.ron`,
// which is the single source of design truth for both; a test asserts they
// stay in lockstep.
Blink(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    max_range: 100.0,
    frontend_specifier: None,
    anchor: Some(BuffSource(PactTalisman)),
    meta: (cooldown: Some(60.0)),
)
